WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:01.870
Ah, technology.

00:00:01.870 --> 00:00:06.750
A double-edged sword of our own making that
can provide both ultimate convenience and

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:10.270
the threat of a grim future ruled by unfeeling
machines.

00:00:10.270 --> 00:00:15.599
Well, maybe the stakes aren’t that high…
yet, but our overreliance on technology can

00:00:15.599 --> 00:00:18.100
have some terrible consequences.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:22.210
The number of traffic accidents continues
to increase year by year, as our main mode

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:26.820
of overland transportation also puts us in
harm’s way for longer and longer portions

00:00:26.820 --> 00:00:28.030
of our day.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:33.750
The internet can allow us to access any information
we may desire, but it can spread misinformation

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:35.550
twice as fast.

00:00:35.550 --> 00:00:37.730
And what about video games?

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:43.360
An interactive artistic medium that can provide
simulated experiences so vivid that many of

00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:46.960
us can eventually lose interest in our real
lives.

00:00:46.960 --> 00:00:52.210
What starts off as a fun indulgence in our
favorite hobby can quickly spiral into an

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:53.210
obsession.

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:57.800
The risks and rewards of virtual space are
satisfyingly predictable compared to the chaos

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:03.750
of modern living, and sometimes we just can’t
stop ourselves from striving for a few more

00:01:03.750 --> 00:01:04.830
easy wins.

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:10.980
Minutes, hours, and even days can go by without
any apparent activity on our side of the screen,

00:01:10.980 --> 00:01:16.160
and yet the world of the video game has changed
drastically due to our actions.

00:01:16.160 --> 00:01:21.440
But, at a certain point, that initial rush
of dopamine wears off, and you find that you

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:26.070
need a much greater challenge in order to
feel any sense of accomplishment.

00:01:26.070 --> 00:01:31.619
So you choose to pick up some harder video
games, and you grind away until you can complete

00:01:31.619 --> 00:01:32.750
them just as easily.

00:01:32.750 --> 00:01:35.220
But that’s not enough either.

00:01:35.220 --> 00:01:39.070
Surely, there must be even tougher games out
there.

00:01:39.070 --> 00:01:41.540
Games that will never go easy on you.

00:01:41.540 --> 00:01:45.530
Games that won’t allow you to make even
a single mistake.

00:01:45.530 --> 00:01:50.810
Games that make you proud of the frankly inexcusable
amount of hours of your life that you’ve

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:56.350
spent sitting in the dark, clutching a controller,
squinting at your screen.

00:01:56.350 --> 00:01:59.850
You need a game that can do all of that and
more.

00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:04.680
And because you’ve effectively given up
your chances at ever being a social butterfly,

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:10.140
you could also use something to help you mitigate
the overwhelming loneliness that now constantly

00:02:10.140 --> 00:02:12.300
defines your everyday life.

00:02:12.300 --> 00:02:19.090
Well, worry no longer – you weary, downtrodden
gamer, you – because here at the SCP Foundation,

00:02:19.090 --> 00:02:25.489
we’ve cooked up a one-of-a-kind mod that
is sure to redefine your gaming experience.

00:02:25.489 --> 00:02:29.860
If this doesn’t turn out to be game of the
year, I don't know what could be.

00:02:29.860 --> 00:02:31.170
Among Us 2, maybe?

00:02:31.170 --> 00:02:34.459
The latest in a long line of Last Of Us Remakes?

00:02:34.459 --> 00:02:36.030
What about Half-Life 3?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:37.379
I digress.

00:02:37.379 --> 00:02:42.900
Introducing the Foundation’s brand new killer
app: the cutting-edge tactical heuristic algorithms

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:51.370
of SCP-1633 combined with the 24/7 companionship
of SCP-1471 Mal0.

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:57.500
I can tell by your expression that you’re
already eager for a playtest, but slow down,

00:02:57.500 --> 00:03:00.640
we need to catch all the normies out there
up to speed.

00:03:00.640 --> 00:03:07.510
Let’s start with the digital canine companion
that is all the rage, SCP-1471 - or should

00:03:07.510 --> 00:03:14.140
I say Ma10 version 1.0.0 - a euclid class
SCP object which comes in the form of a free

00:03:14.140 --> 00:03:16.090
downloadable app for your smartphone.

00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:21.740
There have never been any reviews of this
app for as long as it has existed, but honestly,

00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:25.069
are you really going to trust the words of
a bunch of crooked reviewers when you could

00:03:25.069 --> 00:03:27.120
find out for yourself?

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.129
Words to live by: don’t trust anyone who
isn’t part of your precious gaming hobby.

00:03:32.129 --> 00:03:34.890
The description of Ma10 version 1.0.0.

00:03:34.890 --> 00:03:39.519
reads - Never settle for those awkward feelings
of being alone ever again.

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:45.870
MalO is an exciting and interactive experience
that will keep you engaged and intrigued.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:51.830
The anxiety of social situations can be nerve-racking,
but after just a few hours of MalO you will

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:56.000
soon forget all about those painful emotions
of disappointment.

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:00.360
Be part of the new craze that is quickly becoming
the next social substitute.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:05.270
Remember, the more you participate, the more
MalO will engage you.

00:04:05.270 --> 00:04:08.230
Your experience is completely up to you.

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.470
Absolutely NO ADS.

00:04:10.470 --> 00:04:11.540
Enjoy!

00:04:11.540 --> 00:04:17.380
The app has never received an update, but
that’s because SCP-1471 has been a completely

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.440
functional experience since its release.

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:26.690
All one needs to do is download the app and
within a matter of hours, Ma10 version 1.0.0

00:04:26.690 --> 00:04:30.850
will begin to send the user photographs of
familiar locations.

00:04:30.850 --> 00:04:36.280
These can include photographs of the user's
work, home, or public places they often frequent:

00:04:36.280 --> 00:04:38.730
such as cafes and nightclubs.

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:44.270
In the case of you - a complete shut-in gamer
- these photographs would probably be limited

00:04:44.270 --> 00:04:47.200
to the interior of your favorite gaming room.

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.590
When was the last time you cleaned up those
pizza boxes?

00:04:50.590 --> 00:04:56.300
Regardless of where the images were apparently
taken, each one will contain a canine humanoid

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:58.389
with a skull for a face.

00:04:58.389 --> 00:05:06.430
Say hello to your new best friend, Ma10, or
SCP-1471-A if we’re using the approved designation.

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:12.320
Ma10’s app will continue to send you photographs
for as long as you have it installed, and

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:17.419
because there is no way to uninstall it no
matter how hard you try, you’ll be getting

00:05:17.419 --> 00:05:21.110
intimately close to home selfies for the rest
of your days.

00:05:21.110 --> 00:05:25.530
Doesn’t it feel good to have such a loyal
friend as Ma10?

00:05:25.530 --> 00:05:28.910
Of course, there’s only so much you can
gain from photographs alone.

00:05:28.910 --> 00:05:30.900
You’re a gamer, darn it.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:32.810
And what you want is interactivity!

00:05:32.810 --> 00:05:35.090
But don’t worry about that part.

00:05:35.090 --> 00:05:41.400
We’ve got you more than covered with SCP-1633,
which may, in fact, be the most challenging

00:05:41.400 --> 00:05:44.250
video game ever programmed by mortal hands.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:49.150
Hell, it even gives many games programmed
by anomalous hands a run for their money.

00:05:49.150 --> 00:05:54.000
While it was never released to market and
doesn’t even have a working title, the steampunk

00:05:54.000 --> 00:05:59.900
adventure that awaits you within SCP-1633
is bolstered by highly sophisticated tactical

00:05:59.900 --> 00:06:01.940
heuristic algorithms.

00:06:01.940 --> 00:06:07.900
In this third-person Squad-based action-RPG,
you can switch between four playable characters.

00:06:07.900 --> 00:06:11.259
The Marksman - who specializes in long-range
weaponry

00:06:11.259 --> 00:06:15.310
The Alchemist - with potions and chemicals
to control the battlefield

00:06:15.310 --> 00:06:21.400
The Rogue - a stealth-oriented character who
catches enemies unaware and assassinates them

00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:26.560
And of course, The Thug - a tough-as-nails
melee combatant with increased health and

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:27.560
durability.

00:06:27.560 --> 00:06:32.600
It doesn’t really matter who you choose
because most playthroughs of SCP-1633 always

00:06:32.600 --> 00:06:34.520
end the same way.

00:06:34.520 --> 00:06:39.449
That being said, your hand-eye coordination
and reflexes are second to none, and they

00:06:39.449 --> 00:06:41.750
are also quite possibly your best qualities.

00:06:41.750 --> 00:06:47.030
Let’s set you up with the Marksman as your
main character, since all those shooters you’ve

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:49.430
played will definitely help your aim.

00:06:49.430 --> 00:06:51.960
And trust me, you’re going to need it.

00:06:51.960 --> 00:06:57.849
The story mode of SCP-1633 will put you up
against a slew of victorian-era rascals and

00:06:57.849 --> 00:07:01.669
miscreants, all of which are pulled straight
from the penny dreadfuls.

00:07:01.669 --> 00:07:06.389
There’s even some classic fantasy races
mixed in from the works from good old Professor

00:07:06.389 --> 00:07:10.750
Tolkein himself - dwarves, elves, goblins,
the works.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:16.310
It’s a little generic, but why worry about
the story when the gameplay is what’ll really

00:07:16.310 --> 00:07:17.310
get you hooked.

00:07:17.310 --> 00:07:22.620
There’s a final boss at the end of the game
known as Kr'th'nar trying to destroy the entire

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:26.840
world, you need to stop it - you know, the
usual RPG storyline.

00:07:26.840 --> 00:07:31.590
You’ve stopped dozens of ancient entities,
demon lords, corrupt godlings, and unspeakable

00:07:31.590 --> 00:07:33.460
calamities in your time.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:36.710
This Kr’th’nar will be one more for the
record books.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:37.940
Par for the course.

00:07:37.940 --> 00:07:39.360
Are you ready, player one?

00:07:39.360 --> 00:07:43.880
You’ll be dropped straight into The Marksman’s
shoes, fighting for his and your life against

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:46.190
Kr’th’nar hordes of henchmen.

00:07:46.190 --> 00:07:48.139
But you won’t be doing it alone.

00:07:48.139 --> 00:07:52.810
After all, you’ve got the rest of your squad,
and a mysterious companion whose true intentions

00:07:52.810 --> 00:07:55.229
will reveal themselves in due time.

00:07:55.229 --> 00:07:58.060
We did say we modded the game after all.

00:07:58.060 --> 00:07:59.789
So let’s play.

00:07:59.789 --> 00:08:04.099
Your first two hours won’t be anything to
write home about, not that you ever leave

00:08:04.099 --> 00:08:06.120
your home these days.

00:08:06.120 --> 00:08:11.599
The AI of SCP-1633 will seem to be barely
functioning, a buggy mess where enemies only

00:08:11.599 --> 00:08:14.629
charge in a straight line towards your character.

00:08:14.629 --> 00:08:19.870
Your Marksman will be able to easily take
them down in a hailstorm of projectiles.

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:24.530
At three hours in, things start getting a
bit more interesting as the tactical heuristic

00:08:24.530 --> 00:08:26.060
algorithms kick in.

00:08:26.060 --> 00:08:30.560
The enemies that hold long-range weapons will
shoot at you from a distance, while the close-range

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:35.169
ones move towards you in a serpentine pattern
before attacking in melee.

00:08:35.169 --> 00:08:41.159
This is more like it: not the most challenging,
but the game is clearly increasing in difficulty.

00:08:41.159 --> 00:08:45.590
You also think you see a dark figure with
a skull for a face lurking around corners

00:08:45.590 --> 00:08:47.500
and following your squad.

00:08:47.500 --> 00:08:51.120
But with all the glitches, it’s hard to
tell if this is an intentional part of the

00:08:51.120 --> 00:08:52.399
game or not.

00:08:52.399 --> 00:08:56.720
At five hours, enemies that previously showed
limited signs of strategy are now using cover

00:08:56.720 --> 00:09:02.180
effectively, and will attack with alchemical
splash weapons such as grenades to deal damage

00:09:02.180 --> 00:09:06.930
to your ranged characters and lure your squad
into melee range.

00:09:06.930 --> 00:09:10.579
They still aren’t that much of a challenge,
but the fact that they now exhibit a clear

00:09:10.579 --> 00:09:14.970
self-preservation instinct means that they
are fighting to win.

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.940
This is also when your help officially arrives.

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:22.000
You’re in the middle of a shootout when
you see an enemy about to throw another one

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:24.490
of those frustrating splash weapons.

00:09:24.490 --> 00:09:29.820
You duck behind your cover and prepare to
take a hit, when suddenly the grenade is snatched

00:09:29.820 --> 00:09:35.200
out of the enemy’s hand and tossed in the
opposite direction to explode harmlessly.

00:09:35.200 --> 00:09:42.600
This is the work of SCP-1471-A, who has now
arrived in the game world as an NPC ally.

00:09:42.600 --> 00:09:47.820
For the next several hours of gameplay, Ma10
continues to provide interference by preventing

00:09:47.820 --> 00:09:50.060
any splash weapons from being thrown.

00:09:50.060 --> 00:09:54.959
It’ll sneak up on enemies and take their
weapons, disrupt their cover by pushing movable

00:09:54.959 --> 00:09:59.820
boxes and trash cans out of the way, and even
catch the splash weapons in her mouth like

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:03.360
a dog would catch frisbee before chucking
them away.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:08.730
While it never directly deals damage to the
enemies, its mischievous antics are very efficient

00:10:08.730 --> 00:10:11.140
at protecting you from harm.

00:10:11.140 --> 00:10:15.410
As luck would have it, the enemies can’t
seem to interact with Ma10, and are baffled

00:10:15.410 --> 00:10:19.399
as this invisible force continues to throw
off their strategies.

00:10:19.399 --> 00:10:24.880
Ma10 will use this to its advantage as well
as yours, by appearing at enemy ambush points

00:10:24.880 --> 00:10:29.540
and using sign language to communicate warnings
to you as the player.

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:34.141
Having Ma10 around starts to feel a little
bit like cheating, but keep in mind, the game

00:10:34.141 --> 00:10:38.780
is starting to adapt to your skill level and
will soon begin to employ advanced strategies

00:10:38.780 --> 00:10:40.370
to mess with you.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.310
All the Ma10 mod does is even the playing
field.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.340
The next big leap in enemy intelligence occurs
at the 12 hour mark.

00:10:44.340 --> 00:10:49.480
Kr’th’nar is still running rampant in
the world of SCP-1633 and it's going to take

00:10:49.480 --> 00:10:55.740
your entire squad of steampunk heroes, and
a lonely man’s best friend - Ma10 - to stop

00:10:55.740 --> 00:10:58.240
this big bad evil guy.

00:10:58.240 --> 00:11:02.800
The final boss will possess the highest level
of intelligence that the algorithms are capable

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:07.510
of, and it’ll make that known to you the
second you step into the arena.

00:11:07.510 --> 00:11:12.450
For the majority of your gameplay the enemies
have focused on countering the marksman, since

00:11:12.450 --> 00:11:15.120
you’ve relied on that character’s ranged-weapon
style.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:20.630
But they’ve come to realize that you’re
too much of a pro-MLG gigachad to ever lose

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:26.780
a fair encounter, so Kr’th’nar does the
unthinkable and targets the alchemist, rogue,

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.380
and thug first.

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:32.620
It throws all of its most powerful attacks
at the members of your squad you aren’t

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:36.860
controlling, forcing you to waste resources
in order to keep them alive or switch to them

00:11:36.860 --> 00:11:39.290
in order to dodge fatal blows.

00:11:39.290 --> 00:11:43.290
Whenever you aren’t in command of the marksman,
Kr’th’nar will strike the character with

00:11:43.290 --> 00:11:47.130
a strong melee attack that forces to take
control back.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:52.560
Ma10 is still unable or unwilling to deal
damage to the boss, so it very much seems

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:55.030
like you are on your own.

00:11:55.030 --> 00:11:59.050
Your squad is in shambles, your focus is starting
to wane.

00:11:59.050 --> 00:12:02.970
After all that you’ve been through in this
gaming challenge, it might be the final boss

00:12:02.970 --> 00:12:05.120
that makes you throw in the towel.

00:12:05.120 --> 00:12:07.330
Then, a dialogue box appears.

00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.790
It’s from Ma10.

00:12:08.790 --> 00:12:10.610
Don’t give up hope, user.

00:12:10.610 --> 00:12:15.560
I’ve had so much fun playing with you, and
I know that you have what it takes.

00:12:15.560 --> 00:12:20.449
You never needed a friend before me, and you
can win against Kr’th’nar just like you’ve

00:12:20.449 --> 00:12:23.500
won against every other final boss you’ve
ever faced.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:24.889
You got this, buddy.

00:12:24.889 --> 00:12:26.570
Your best friend, MA10

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:32.360
It felt overly sentimental, but something
about this message fills you with the determination

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:33.670
to keep going.

00:12:33.670 --> 00:12:39.120
You call upon all of your gaming knowledge,
all of your skill, all of your passion, and

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:44.340
with pinpoint precision, you guide your squad
to defeat Kr’th’nar in record-breaking

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:45.340
time.

00:12:45.340 --> 00:12:50.290
You sit back in your gaming chair, exhilarated
and finally satisfied.

00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:55.930
This truly was the ultimate gaming experience,
and all you needed was a little help from

00:12:55.930 --> 00:12:56.930
your friend.

00:12:56.930 --> 00:13:07.600
Now go check out SCP-1471 - MalO Version 1.0.0
and What if SCP-1471 MalO Was Put Inside SCP-914?

00:13:07.600 --> 00:13:11.080
For more absurd Mal0 antics to brighten your
day!

